---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import { site } from '../../site.config';
import { latest, coins, avgFx, avgUsdt, btc, kst } from '../../lib/data';
import { fmtPct } from '../../lib/calc.mjs';
import { fit } from '../../lib/text';

const fx = latest.fx;
const title = fit(['Kimchi Premium Today: Upbit vs Binance, Coin by Coin', 'Kimchi Premium Today: Upbit vs Binance by Coin (KRW)'], 50, 60);
const description = fit([
  `Korean-language board comparing Upbit KRW prices with Binance USDT prices for ${coins.length} coins, using the ECB USD/KRW reference rate and Upbit's USDT price. English summary.`,
  `Korean board comparing Upbit KRW prices with Binance USDT prices for ${coins.length} coins, using the ECB USD/KRW reference rate and Upbit's USDT price. English summary page.`,
  `Korean board comparing Upbit KRW and Binance USDT prices for ${coins.length} coins, against both the ECB USD/KRW reference rate and Upbit's USDT price. English summary.`,
], 150, 160);
const top = [...coins].sort((a, b) => b.upbitVolumeKrw24h - a.upbitVolumeKrw24h).slice(0, 8);
const page = { '@context': 'https://schema.org', '@type': 'WebPage', name: title, url: `${site.url}/en/`, inLanguage: 'en', dateModified: latest.asOf, about: { '@id': `${site.url}/#org` } };
---
<Base title={title} description={description} path="/en/" og="en" lang="en" ld={[page]} crumbs={[{ name: 'English', path: '/en/' }]} modified={latest.asOf}>
  <article class="doc" lang="en">
    <h1>What is the kimchi premium right now?</h1>
    <p class="answer" id="answer">At the {kst(latest.asOf)} reading, the average premium across {coins.length} coins was {fmtPct(avgFx)} against the ECB reference rate (1 USD = {fx.usdKrw} KRW, published {fx.usdKrwDate}) and {fmtPct(avgUsdt)} against Upbit's USDT price ({fx.usdtKrw} KRW). Bitcoin: {fmtPct(btc.premiumFx)} / {fmtPct(btc.premiumUsdt)}.</p>
    <div class="prose">
      <p>This site is written in Korean. This page is a short English summary of what it measures; the full board is on the <a href="/" hreflang="ko">Korean home page</a> and every coin has its own <a href="/coins/" hreflang="ko">coin page</a>.</p>
      <h2>How is the premium calculated?</h2>
      <p>Premium = Upbit KRW price ÷ (Binance USDT price × KRW per dollar) − 1. We show two bases: the ECB euro reference rates cross-converted to USD/KRW via the Frankfurter API, and Upbit's own KRW-USDT market price. The gap between the two numbers is roughly the "tether premium" ({fmtPct(fx.tetherPremium)} in this reading). Full formulas and sources are on the <a href="/methodology/" hreflang="ko">methodology page</a> (Korean).</p>
      <h2>Largest Upbit markets in this reading</h2>
      <div class="table-scroll">
        <table>
          <caption>Snapshot {kst(latest.asOf)}. Sources: Upbit Open API, Binance public spot data, Frankfurter (ECB).</caption>
          <thead><tr><th scope="col">Coin</th><th scope="col">Upbit (KRW)</th><th scope="col">Binance (USDT)</th><th scope="col">vs ECB rate</th><th scope="col">vs USDT</th></tr></thead>
          <tbody>
            {top.map((c) => (
              <tr><th scope="row"><a href={`/coins/${c.symbol.toLowerCase()}/`} hreflang="ko">{c.nameEn} ({c.symbol})</a></th><td class="num">{c.upbitKrw.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td class="num">{c.binanceUsdt.toLocaleString('en-US')}</td><td class={`num ${c.premiumFx >= 0 ? 'up' : 'down'}`}>{fmtPct(c.premiumFx)}</td><td class={`num ${c.premiumUsdt >= 0 ? 'up' : 'down'}`}>{fmtPct(c.premiumUsdt)}</td></tr>
            ))}
          </tbody>
        </table>
      </div>
      <h2>What this site is not</h2>
      <p>It is not investment or arbitrage advice and carries no exchange referral links. Moving funds between Korean and overseas exchanges is subject to Korean foreign-exchange rules, the travel rule and tax; read the <a href="/disclaimer/" hreflang="ko">disclaimer</a>. Contact: <a href={`mailto:${site.contactEmail}`}>{site.contactEmail}</a>.</p>
    </div>
  </article>
</Base>
